 The package uses PSTricks to fit curves to:

-    Linear Functions;
-    Power Functions;
-    exp Function;
-    Log_{10} and Log_e functions;
-    Recip;
-    Kings Law data;
-    Gaussian; and
-    4th order Polynomial

It also prints regression statistics, draws confidence and
prediction intervals and standardised residuals, and has a
plot style for error bars with a calculated length.

With the option bignum the fit is calculated with decimal
numbers of arbitrary precision. This is for polynomials of a
high order with dvips and Ghostscript; with LuaLaTeX the option
is ignored. The decimal numbers come from the package pst-numeric
if it is installed, otherwise from the header file pst-fit-bignum.pro,
which has to be installed in dvips/pst-fit/ of a TeX tree.

